<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Bruttii</h1><p class="st-meta">356 BCE – 203 BCE (approx.) · capital Consentia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Oscan-speaking people who broke away from the Lucanians in 356 BCE and dominated the toe of Italy, Hannibal's last stronghold.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diodorus-siculus">Diodorus</a> says that in 356 BCE runaway slaves and herdsmen in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, then under Lucanian control, rebelled and formed a new people, the Bruttii. The story may simplify a revolt of a subject population, but by the late 4th century BCE they were an independent federation.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosenza">Consentia</a> (Cosenza). They lived in hill towns and drew wealth from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sila-calabria">Sila</a> forest, producing pitch and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a>. They captured Greek cities including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hipponion">Hipponion</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terina">Terina</a> and minted fine coins. They fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-epirus">Alexander of Epirus</a> and joined Pyrrhus against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> subdued them by 270 BCE and took half the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sila-calabria">Sila</a>. They joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> after Cannae, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruttium">Bruttium</a> was his last base in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> until he left in 203 BCE. As punishment they lost land and status; Roman writers said they were reduced to serving as attendants to magistrates.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 356 BCE – 203 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:52.62%;width:3.04%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>356 BCE – 203 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Consentia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Oscan polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oscan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bruttians, Bruttian League</dd></dl></aside></div>
